# `{ ...parcel }` in a loop: the literal was filled behind tests of ONE key order, and the first parcel of another order left the typed copy of the loop for good.
# A pure copy of the literal's own layout goes by the cell's words, whatever the order, as it did outside loops.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true
# CHECK: TryCopyFields
# RUN(ORDERS): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# ORDERS-LABEL: code f1:Body
# ORDERS-NOT: HasKeyOrder
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# ANSWERS: 4 [{"weight":1,"fragile":2},{"weight":3,"insured":4},{"weight":1,"fragile":2},{"weight":3,"insured":4}]
